            <ArticleTitle>Driving out the 'toothworm' in today's China.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For thousands of years people have tried to explain toothache as the result of a worm residing in a carious tooth. Fumigation of the carious tooth, with the smoke from burning henbane or leek seeds, was used to drive the &quot;toothworm&quot; out of the tooth. A quack in modern China adopted the same ruse and supposedly drove the worms out of student's tooth. This duplicitous procedure was captured on film by a dentist who witnessed it.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
